From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Read the version resource from the file when the mapped image has none.

GetFileVersionInfoSize/GetFileVersionInfo map the file with LOAD_LIBRARY_AS_IMAGE_RESOURCE. For a dll in system32,
ntdll swaps that image mapping for Wine's builtin (default load order), so the version of a native dll that sits
there (Microsoft's vcruntime140.dll, concrt140.dll, msvcp140_1.dll 14.51) read as "no resource" (error 1812):
Wine's builtins of those carry none. Windows reads the file on disk. msi then compared such files by size, overwrote
the prefix's 14.51 runtime with Acrobat's bundled 14.44 and, when the install failed, deleted it (see 0094): every
Adobe app stopped starting (c0000135). When the mapped image has no version resource, the file is now read directly
(the existing path for files that do not load).
Test: a small GetFileVersionInfoW probe on system32\vcruntime140/concrt140/msvcp140_1: 1812 before, 14.51.36247.0
after; kernel32 unchanged (10.0.19045.5796). Acrobat 26.002 MSI on a clean prefix: "keeping vcruntime140 (new
version 14.44.35211.0 old version 14.51.36247.0)", as Windows.
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/version.c b/dlls/kernelbase/version.c
index 809577a..1327b86 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/version.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/version.c
@@ -791,7 +791,9 @@ DWORD WINAPI GetFileVersionInfoSizeExW( DWORD flags, LPCWSTR filename, LPDWORD r
         }
         FreeLibrary( hModule );
     }
-    else
+    /* Mapping a system32 dll as an image resource maps Wine's builtin in its place (load order), which may carry no
+     * version resource. Windows reads the file on disk, so read it directly when the mapped image had none. */
+    if (magic == 1)
     {
         HANDLE handle = CreateFileW( filename, GENERIC_READ, FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_WRITE,
                                      NULL, OPEN_EXISTING, 0, 0 );
@@ -899,7 +901,9 @@ BOOL WINAPI GetFileVersionInfoExW( DWORD flags, LPCWSTR filename, DWORD ignored,
         }
         FreeLibrary( hModule );
     }
-    else
+    /* Mapping a system32 dll as an image resource maps Wine's builtin in its place (load order), which may carry no
+     * version resource. Windows reads the file on disk, so read it directly when the mapped image had none. */
+    if (magic == 1)
     {
         HANDLE handle = CreateFileW( filename, GENERIC_READ, FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_WRITE,
                                      NULL, OPEN_EXISTING, 0, 0 );
